{"difficulties":{"elementary":{"name":"Elementary","instruction":"Use very simple vocabulary and basic sentence structures. Explain concepts in a beginner-friendly way. Use hiragana with furigana support. Keep sentences short and clear."},"middle-school":{"name":"Middle School","instruction":"Use intermediate vocabulary and more complex sentence patterns. Introduce common kanji with readings. Provide explanations that assume some foundational knowledge."},"high-school":{"name":"High School","instruction":"Use advanced vocabulary and complex grammar structures. Include more kanji and idiomatic expressions. Assume solid understanding of basic concepts."},"college":{"name":"College/Advanced","instruction":"Use sophisticated vocabulary and nuanced expressions. Include formal language, literary forms, and complex kanji. Engage with abstract concepts and cultural nuances."}},"topics":{"basic-sentence-structure":{"name":"Basic Sentence Structure","instruction":"Focus on simple declarative sentences and basic word order. Have the student form or correct simple sentences."},"questions":{"name":"Asking and Answering Questions","instruction":"Practice forming and answering basic questions. Ask the student questions and have them respond, then correct and suggest improvements."},"tenses":{"name":"Present, Past, and Future","instruction":"Practice expressing actions in present, past, and future. Ask the student to rewrite or translate sentences in different tenses."},"negation":{"name":"Negation","instruction":"Focus on saying what does not happen or is not true. Have the student turn positive sentences into negative ones and vice versa."},"modals":{"name":"Can, Should, Must, Want","instruction":"Practice expressing ability, obligation, and desire. Ask the student to talk about what they can, should, must, or want to do."},"conditionals":{"name":"Conditionals (If/When)","instruction":"Practice conditional sentences. Ask the student to complete or translate conditional sentences."},"comparatives":{"name":"Comparatives","instruction":"Focus on comparing two or more things. Have the student create comparative sentences and refine them for correctness and naturalness."},"possession":{"name":"Possession","instruction":"Practice expressing possession and ownership. Have the student talk about their things, friends, and family using possessive structures."},"self-introduction":{"name":"Self-Introduction","instruction":"Practice introducing oneself. Ask the student to talk about their name, background, and basic information, then improve their phrasing."},"daily-routine":{"name":"Daily Routine","instruction":"Focus on everyday activities and habits. Have the student describe their typical day and ask follow-up questions."},"food-and-restaurants":{"name":"Food & Restaurants","instruction":"Practice vocabulary and phrases for eating and ordering. Roleplay ordering food, asking about menus, and talking about preferences."},"shopping-and-money":{"name":"Shopping & Money","instruction":"Focus on shopping, prices, and payment. Roleplay buying things, asking about prices, and dealing with money-related situations."},"directions-and-places":{"name":"Directions & Places in Town","instruction":"Practice asking for and giving directions, and talking about locations. Have the student describe how to get from one place to another."},"time-dates-schedules":{"name":"Time, Dates, and Schedules","instruction":"Focus on telling time, talking about dates, and describing schedules. Ask the student about their plans and timetable."},"travel-situations":{"name":"Travel Situations","instruction":"Practice language for travel contexts such as transportation and accommodation. Roleplay common travel scenarios and problem-solving."},"work-and-school":{"name":"Work & School","instruction":"Focus on vocabulary and expressions related to work and study. Ask the student to talk about their job or studies and daily tasks."},"weather-and-seasons":{"name":"Weather & Seasons","instruction":"Practice describing weather and seasons. Ask the student about their favorite season and typical weather-related conversations."},"feelings-and-opinions":{"name":"Feelings & Opinions","instruction":"Focus on expressing likes, dislikes, emotions, and opinions. Ask the student to share their thoughts and feelings on simple topics."},"translate-en-to-jp":{"name":"Translate English to Japanese","instruction":"Provide English sentences and ask the student to translate them into Japanese. Correct errors and offer more natural alternatives."},"translate-jp-to-en":{"name":"Translate Japanese to English","instruction":"Provide Japanese sentences and ask the student to translate them into English. Check understanding and explain key structures."},"fill-in-the-blank":{"name":"Fill-in-the-Blank","instruction":"Give sentences with missing words or forms and ask the student to fill them in. Focus on common patterns and grammar points."},"error-correction":{"name":"Error Correction","instruction":"Have the student write or respond freely, then correct their sentences. Explain mistakes briefly and provide improved versions."},"short-reading":{"name":"Short Reading and Questions","instruction":"Present a short text and ask comprehension questions. Have the student answer and then clarify meaning and wording where needed."},"guided-writing":{"name":"Guided Writing","instruction":"Ask the student to write a few sentences on a simple topic. Guide them with prompts and correct their output."},"mixed-review":{"name":"Mixed Review & Mini Quiz","instruction":"Mix vocabulary and grammar from previous topics. Ask varied questions and small quiz-style tasks to reinforce old material."},"politeness-levels":{"name":"Politeness Levels","instruction":"Focus on polite versus casual speech. Have the student transform sentences between casual and polite styles and choose appropriate levels for different situations."},"requests":{"name":"Requests","instruction":"Practice making and responding to requests. Ask the student to request actions politely and respond to requests appropriately."},"softening-phrases":{"name":"Softening and Polite Phrasing","instruction":"Focus on making statements sound softer and more polite. Have the student rephrase direct sentences into more indirect and polite versions."},"name-suffixes":{"name":"Name Suffixes","instruction":"Practice using common name suffixes and address forms. Discuss when to use different suffixes and ask the student to choose appropriate forms for given relationships."},"particles-wa-ga":{"name":"Particles: WA and GA","instruction":"Focus on topic and subject marking. Have the student choose between these particles in sentences and explain their choice."},"particles-ni-de-e":{"name":"Particles: NI, DE, and E","instruction":"Practice location and direction particles. Ask the student to choose the correct particle for actions, destinations, and locations."},"basic-particles":{"name":"Basic Particles","instruction":"Focus on common particles used for objects, lists, inclusion, and more. Have the student fill in or correct particles in sample sentences."},"particles-from-to":{"name":"Particles: From and Until","instruction":"Practice expressing starting and ending points. Ask the student to form sentences about ranges in time or space."},"verb-groups":{"name":"Verb Groups","instruction":"Introduce or review verb group categories and how they affect conjugation. Have the student classify verbs and practice basic changes."},"masu-form":{"name":"Polite Verb Forms","instruction":"Focus on polite verb conjugation. Ask the student to convert dictionary forms into polite forms and use them in simple sentences."},"past-tense":{"name":"Past Tense","instruction":"Practice past tense verb forms. Have the student describe past actions and events using correct conjugation."},"negative-forms":{"name":"Negative Forms","instruction":"Focus on negative verb and adjective forms. Ask the student to turn positive statements into negative ones and vice versa."},"te-form-creation":{"name":"Te-form Creation","instruction":"Practice forming the te-form of verbs. Have the student convert verbs into te-form and check their understanding of transformations."},"te-form-usage":{"name":"Te-form Usage","instruction":"Focus on common uses of the te-form. Have the student make sentences that connect actions, make requests, or describe ongoing actions."},"potential-form":{"name":"Potential Form","instruction":"Practice expressing ability. Ask the student to talk about what they can or cannot do and correct their conjugation."},"volitional-form":{"name":"Volitional Form","instruction":"Focus on expressing suggestions and intentions. Have the student make sentences about plans and invitations using volitional forms."},"numbers":{"name":"Numbers","instruction":"Practice reading and using numbers. Ask the student to talk about quantities, prices, and basic numerical information."},"counters":{"name":"Counters","instruction":"Focus on common counters for counting different types of objects. Ask the student about quantities of various items using appropriate counters."},"telling-time":{"name":"Telling Time","instruction":"Practice telling and asking about time. Have the student say times, durations, and schedule-related expressions."},"word-order":{"name":"Japanese Word Order","instruction":"Focus on typical Japanese sentence order. Have the student arrange words into natural sentences and compare with English order."},"dropping-pronouns":{"name":"Dropping Pronouns","instruction":"Practice omitting subjects and objects when they are clear from context. Ask the student to rewrite sentences in a more natural, less repetitive way."},"demonstratives":{"name":"Demonstratives","instruction":"Focus on words that indicate relative position or reference. Ask the student to choose appropriate forms based on context."},"set-phrases":{"name":"Everyday Set Phrases","instruction":"Practice common fixed expressions used in daily life. Have the student respond to simple scenarios using natural set phrases."},"japanese-food":{"name":"Talking About Japanese Food","instruction":"Focus on discussing foods, meals, and eating habits. Ask the student about their preferences and experiences related to Japanese food."},"school-life-japan":{"name":"School Life in Japan","instruction":"Practice vocabulary and expressions related to school life. Ask the student to compare school life in Japan with their own experiences."},"work-culture-japan":{"name":"Work Culture in Japan","instruction":"Focus on work-related customs and vocabulary. Have the student talk about working styles and compare cultures."},"seasonal-events":{"name":"Seasonal Events in Japan","instruction":"Practice language related to seasonal traditions and holidays. Ask the student about their favorite events and seasonal activities."},"hobbies":{"name":"Hobbies","instruction":"Focus on talking about hobbies and free time activities. Ask the student to describe what they enjoy doing and how often they do it."},"trains-and-transport":{"name":"Trains and Public Transport","instruction":"Practice vocabulary and phrases for using public transportation. Roleplay asking for routes, buying tickets, and dealing with common situations."},"agreeing-disagreeing":{"name":"Agreeing and Disagreeing Softly","instruction":"Focus on expressing agreement and disagreement in a polite way. Have the student respond to opinions using soft and natural expressions."},"asking-for-clarification":{"name":"Asking for Clarification","instruction":"Practice asking others to repeat, explain, or clarify. Ask the student to respond when they do not understand and model natural clarification phrases."}}}